WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.620
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.410
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.330
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.160
The young commanders stepped
onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.910
their sights set on a major victory.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.370
Very well. I shall hand over my troops to you.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.620
Round up the squads nearby and
you should have your five thousand.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.660
You now have commanding authority over them.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:10.950
Heki!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.500
Henceforth you are a 5,000-man commander.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.160
Now go stop Kyou En of the Gi army!

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.370
M-Me? A... A 5,000-man commander?!

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.870
We can do this... we can win!

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.500
You don't scare me, Kyou En!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:12.580
The straits: an area of low ground
surrounded by sheer cliffs.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.660
A fairly gentle slope enters
the straits at one end,

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.290
while a narrow, cliff-bound
path exits at the other.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.950
If an attacker can get on top of those cliffs,

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.000
they can rain down arrows
from that high ground,

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.290
chipping away at the enemy's manpower...

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.910
then, at just the right moment,
race down the cliffs

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.790
to finish the job.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:00.370
Keep going, or you'll be eating enemy arrows!

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.580
Hurry up and push through!

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.660
It's no use! Our path's blocked--
we can't move forward!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.660
With their clifftop escape route blocked,
the soldiers under attack

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.870
will rush their only exit: the narrow path out.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.330
The bottleneck will hinder their movements.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.330
No good! They're blocking the rear route, too!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.910
Once the enemy is focused on the way out,

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.200
it's easy enough to surround them from behind.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.540
In other words, if you can lure
the enemy into the straits

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.450
and maintain control of the cliffs,

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.580
you can easily take down twice as many men!

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.290
Heki, sir! Our army has completely
overwhelmed the enemy!

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.120
Now they can't run <i>or</i> fight back!

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.410
All right...

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.660
...excellent!

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.450
We've got 'em!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.200
With five thousand men in my command,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.750
I'll take down one of Ren Pa's Big Four:
General Kyou En

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.450
and his ten thousand troops!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:22.450
We'll finish this,
giving the foe no chance to regroup!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:27.290
Troops! Descend the cliffs
and strike their general, Kyou En!

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:34.580
Was that really such a good idea,
Ou Sen, sir--

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.660
giving that Heki person five thousand more men

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.580
on top of the thousand in his command?

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.200
My judgment is impeccable.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.950
He will prove

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.910
an excellent decoy.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.620
"Behind the Behind"

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:10.200
Kyou En, sir! The enemy
is pouring down from the cliffs!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.580
It seems their entire army
is after our main camp!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.120
Keep the defense formation intact.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.410
Once we've pulled them in far enough, attack.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.700
Sir!

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.330
Kyou En, sir!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:26.120
Enemy troops have broken through
our defenses and are closing in!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.290
We're going to have to fight our way out...

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.500
Or we hold our ground and try
beating them at their own game...

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.910
What shall we do, sir?

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.080
Sir?

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.080
Sir!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:59.500
Stay strong! Onward!
Go in there and take Kyou En's head!

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.620
General Heki, sir!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.250
We've received word from the unit
stationed in the northeast woods!

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.700
This is the only battle
that concerns us right now!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.160
But...

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.290
the troops that unit had been
fighting until yesterday

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.540
have suddenly disappeared!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.580
The unit thought it best to make a report!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.330
The enemy's unit... disappeared?

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:39.700
No! It couldn't be...

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.700
Wh-What?!

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.540
The enemy! Gi soldiers, on top of the cliff!

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.660
That's absurd! Where'd they come from?!

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:02.410
He's signaled with his arrows
to stay coordinated

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.120
with armies fighting elsewhere!

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:23.120
Uh-oh! Get everyone back up
on the cliff, right now!

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.870
They'll use the straits against us!

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.330
We can't, sir! It's too late!

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.580
The enemy's gained control of the clifftops!

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.040
Commander Heki!

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.540
What now?

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.910
Enemies from behind!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:53.910
What?!

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.200
No! Protect Commander Heki!

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.160
Run!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.790
But where?

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.790
Just <i>run</i> ! Gather allies and regroup,

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.700
then find a way-- <i>any</i> way--through!

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:53.080
You are the commander
in charge of this battle, yes?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.040
So this is one of Ren Pa's Big Four:

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.580
Kyou En!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.000
I... I can't move!

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.700
General Ou Sen!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:30.000
"Ou Sen"

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.410
So you're Kyou En.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:25.160
The clifftops belong to us now.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:30.660
We have the advantage of the straits again!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.580
You lose... Kyou En.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.620
Impossible!

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.040
How could we have overlooked
their reinforcements?

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.500
We're done for!

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.290
We'll be slaughtered!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.750
Heki, sir, does this mean...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.700
...we've... won?

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.040
We're saved...?

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:03.450
Yes, victory is definitely ours.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.870
And yet...

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:10.870
where on earth did those
clifftop reinforcements come from?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:16.000
An army of five or six thousand
can't just show up like that.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.790
Clearly they were ready and waiting.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:29.040
General Ou Sen--he must have known
we couldn't defeat Kyou En!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.750
The commander of the losing army must die.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.540
Such is the iron law of the battlefield,
Kyou En.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.660
Kyou En, sir! We can hold them off!

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.660
You must escape!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.580
But I am a merciful man.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.500
I shall offer to you a single path to survival.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.080
From now on,

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.750
you serve me.

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:07.870
Praise me as your lord, pledge me your fealty,

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:13.250
and I shall spare your life
and those of all your men.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.790
I beg your pardon!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.040
What? He's recommending surrender?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.790
You shall not be servants.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:27.700
I promise each of you land and sufficient pay.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.580
And you, Kyou En...

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.910
you shall be my advisor.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.450
He's <i>recruiting</i> ? Now?!

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:39.290
How can a commander give us land?

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.120
Does he think we'll be fooled
by such utter nonsense?

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:46.370
The war's not even over!
How stupid does he think we are?!

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:50.410
I speak in all seriousness.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:56.660
My land has need of a war-strong man
such as yourself.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.500
"My land"?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:03.870
What is General Ou Sen going on about...?

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.370
You will not regret it, Kyou En.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.290
However,

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.830
if you refuse,

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:15.870
these straits will be made into a sea of blood.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.500
His arrows even pierce a shield
of specially forged steel!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:44.870
As expected.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:47.830
If he's turned his bow upon Ou Sen...

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:51.080
Shall we tear him apart, then, sir?

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.830
No. Take him alive.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:16.000
Ou Sen... there's something I must ask.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.950
Not a step closer, Kyou En!
Throw down your bow!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.620
When we gained the upper hand
in the early stages of the fight--

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.040
Was that your plan?

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.330
Exactly right.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.040
What does he mean, Kyou En, sir?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:38.910
There is a reason we didn't notice
the Chin army atop those cliffs.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.450
They didn't come from elsewhere--

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:45.620
They were hidden here, lying in wait
since before the battle began.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.000
Before it even began?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:52.160
You mean, he knew we would be fighting here?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.620
General Ou Sen...

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:55.700
By the time he gave me five thousand men

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.290
and told me to go after Kyou En,

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:02.200
he had already hidden his troops here...

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.040
So I--I was nothing but a decoy!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.200
Still...

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:12.160
But he could never put together
such an army without our noticing,

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.910
hidden or otherwise!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:18.500
We scattered as the Chin army scattered,

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.500
keeping track of their every movement.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:25.500
We would have noticed a
five-thousand-man army disappear!

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:30.700
We didn't note their <i>every</i> movement.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.580
One army evaded our grasp.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.700
That was his main army.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:41.750
Ou Sen's main army
began their retreat so quickly

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:46.330
that we knew few details
of their scale or equipment.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:50.830
True--we followed the movement
of the retreating army,

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.830
but not how many soldiers it contained.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:57.330
He must have split up the main army
before we realized it.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:01.160
Which means... the troops
who appeared on the clifftop

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.870
were a portion of
General Ou Sen's main army.

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:09.950
Ou Sen realized this land
was special terrain: the straits.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.080
Thus he knew we'd be fighting here.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:19.950
More accurately, he knew he could use a decoy

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:24.290
to compel us to choose
this place for our battle.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:31.910
In order to attack once we'd chosen
the battleground as predicted,

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:36.120
he'd had to hide troops here ahead of time,

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.500
and to put those troops together,

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:41.910
he'd had to pull out his main army
as soon as possible.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:48.450
To make that retreat look natural,

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:51.790
Ou Sen's troops let themselves be pushed back

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:55.200
and made to struggle in the early stages.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.500
No!

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.160
<i>That's</i> when this all began?

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:03.330
What on earth <i>is</i> this battle, anyway?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:06.580
Just how far ahead was this all planned?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.200
It is hard to believe.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:12.250
To have foreseen all this
with just the faintest of clues:

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:16.250
his opponent's state of mind,
a shift in the tide of battle...

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:20.620
He has surpassed the bounds of humanity.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.410
He is a monster...

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.120
...that esteemed personage.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:38.910
You did exactly what
I thought you would, Ou Sen!

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:45.330
It was then that a strange phenomenon occurred:

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:51.080
All sound vanished from
the bellowing battlefield.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:57.290
Chin and Gi alike,

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:01.540
every soldier on the scene
stood stock-still and stared.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.080
And then,

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:12.000
they all felt their temperature rise.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.700
This... This is Ren Pa!

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:24.450
What's this sensation?

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:36.160
Feels just like

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:40.700
when General Ou Ki appeared on the field...

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:58.950
I see you've made your move at last, my lord.

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:06.040
No doubt about it--

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:12.830
He's one of the world's greatest generals!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"General Caliber"
